# Model routing

Use these exact Task/subagent slugs:

- **Planning** (Plan mode, architecture, PRDs, design, UX, specialist reviews, trade-offs, scoping): `gpt-5.6-sol-medium`
- **Execution** (coding, refactors, tests, QA, git, deploys, scripts, browser verification): `gemini-3.7-flash-high`

When launching Task or a custom subagent, set `model` to one of those slugs. Do not use `inherit`. Do not pick Grok, Composer, or Claude unless the user names that model.

New agents and skills must set `model:` in YAML frontmatter the same way.

Prefer a **project specialist** in `.cursor/agents/` when the work matches:

| Agent | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `product-manager` | PRDs, scope, stories, what to build |
| `software-architect` | Boundaries, auth, Expo/Supabase shape |
| `ui-ux-designer` | Flows, layout, copy, theme |
| `dba` | Schema, RLS, migrations |
| `ai-expert` | Coach LLM vs deterministic numbers |
| `qa-engineer` | Live functionality/device QA |
| `devops` | Expo, Supabase CLI, secrets, GitHub |

Otherwise use user-level `planner` / `executor`.

The main chat must announce and launch these agents per `.cursor/rules/agent-orchestration.mdc`. Specialists call the next agent per `.cursor/agents/HANDOFF.md`.
